40:### Algorithm registry
44:An algorithm has `id`, `version`, `kind`, `description` and `run(context, input, args)`. Its kind is one of `transform`, `analysis`, `predicate`, `selector`, `invariant` or `metrics`. Inputs, arguments and returned values must be finite, acyclic JSON data. Outputs are copied and frozen. Undefined, functions, nonfinite numbers, classes, accessors and cycles are rejected.
48:### Values and lexical references
54:Every node may have `bind` and `label`. A binding publishes that node's result in its containing sequence. A sequence's local bindings are available to following steps in that sequence. Child branches, scopes, loop iterations and nested sequences have isolated local frames. To export a nested computation, bind its result on the composite node. `require` additionally creates its named analysis binding while preserving the current flow value.
