10 01-sketch-guide-rewrite-search-on-ssa-and-verified-rules.md 87 ## 2. Value trees: the unit everything here rewrites  The main IR, `typed.blocks` (`src/typed/model.ts`), is a control-flow graph of blocks. A block holds statements, and a statement holds **value trees**. A statement is one of eight operations (`set` a local, `store` to memory, `eval`, `br`, `br_if`, `return`, `trap`, `zero`). A value is a node with one of 54 operators (`ValueOp`, `model.ts:35`): `const`, `get` (read a local), integer arithmetic and comparisons, loads, `call`, the f32 operators and a few addressing forms. 
11 01-sketch-guide-image-level-contracts-for-float-freedom.md 119 ## 5. Contracts, and where a tolerance would plug in  A sampled check is a `DifferentialSpec` (`src/framework/contracts/differential.ts:31`): ports, a baseline and a subject, a case generator, `run`, and a `compare(baseline, subject, case)` that returns `true` or `{ ok, reason }` (`CaseComparison`, `:26`). Its evidence records how many cases agreed, disagreed or were inconclusive. `assuranceOf(evidence)` (`:325`) maps a sampled check to `checked-sampled` and anything else to `checked-exact`. The vocabulary has no entry for "within a bound". 
