30 01-parallel-terms-with-a-serial-fold-and-a-launch-time-gate-for-fusion.md 45 ## Term staging  **Where.** In a block-mode group, a member with no trailing axes (rank = block depth: `mean[i]`, `s[i]`) has one element per block and thread 0 computes it. For each *outermost* reduction R of such a member (a reduction not inside another reduction), the plan decides whether R's terms are staged. 
